---
/** Custom time → a cron expression, explained in plain words before it's saved. */
import ZedWindow from "../zed/ZedWindow.astro";
import Caption from "./Caption.astro";
---

<figure class="scene not-content" data-scene data-steps="1800,2800,3200,3800">
  <ZedWindow title="Release notes" label="Rewake" label2="Rewake (1)" labelAt={3} height={360}>
    <div class="zed-form" data-at={1} data-until={2}>
      <header>Input Requested by Claude Agent</header>
      <div class="q">Custom time: type a cron expression (minute hour day month weekday), in your local time.</div>
      <div class="f"><span>Cron expression</span><div class="input zed-code">0 9 * * 1-5</div></div>
      <div class="actions"><span class="zed-btn ok"><i>✓</i> Submit</span><span class="zed-btn no"><i>✕</i> Decline</span><span class="zed-btn">Cancel</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="zed-form" data-at={2} data-until={3}>
      <header>Input Requested by Claude Agent</header>
      <div class="q">Rewake understood "0 9 * * 1-5" as: Every weekday (Monday to Friday) at 9:00 AM. Next runs: 9:00 AM tomorrow (Tuesday); Wednesday at 9:00 AM; Thursday at 9:00 AM.</div>
      <div class="f">
        <span>How often</span>
        <div class="radio on">Every time it matches</div>
        <div class="radio">Only once (9:00 AM tomorrow (Tuesday))</div>
      </div>
      <div class="actions"><span class="zed-btn ok"><i>✓</i> Submit</span><span class="zed-btn no"><i>✕</i> Decline</span><span class="zed-btn">Cancel</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="zed-user" data-until={1}>Every weekday morning, summarise yesterday's merged PRs for the changelog.</div>
    <div class="zed-status" data-at={3}>Rewake: Scheduled for 9:00 AM tomorrow (Tuesday). Repeats: Every weekday (Monday to Friday) at 9:00 AM. To change it, use the Rewake menu under the message box.</div>
  </ZedWindow>
  <Caption>Repeat hourly, daily, on weekdays, or on any cron schedule. Rewake reads it back in plain words, with the next three runs, before anything is saved.</Caption>
</figure>
